# ── generated testing artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both are OUTPUT. The generators are committed; these are not.
#
# The collection is ~300KB regenerated from docs/api/openapi.yaml, so committing
# it means a large diff every time a route changes — and a stale copy is worse
# than none, because a request that 404s reads as a bug in the service rather
# than as a file nobody re-ran. `node testing/build-postman.mjs` rebuilds it,
# and tests/contract/openapi.test.ts already fails if the spec drifts from the
# registered routes, so the regenerated file is correct by construction.
#
# The environment file exists to hold ids minted by testing/bootstrap.mjs —
# INCLUDING A PLAINTEXT API KEY, which the API returns exactly once. It is
# local-only and worthless against any deployment, but a committed file whose
# purpose is to carry a credential is a habit worth not forming, and it trips
# secret scanners. Re-run bootstrap.mjs to mint a fresh one.
testing/outreach.postman_collection.json
testing/outreach.postman_environment.json

